<title>THAILAND: Thai Petrochem exports fuel to Singapore.</title>
<headline>Thai Petrochem exports fuel to Singapore.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Petrochemical Industry Plc on Thursday exported 55 million litres of low-sulphur fuel oil to Singapore, a company official said today.</p>
<p>Next week, the company will export 35 million litres of high octane gasoline to South Korea and kerosene to Japan, the official said.</p>
<p>TPI operates a condensate splitter with capacity of 65,000 barrels per day. The refinery started operation in April and has already reached full capacity.</p>
<p>The refinery produced feedstocks for TPI's petrochemical industry, the official added.</p>
<p>Other company's clients included Vietnam, Laos, China and Cambodia, the official said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
